{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "WRFWeselyData",
    "description": "Tables of WRF-Chem's Wesely dry-deposition scheme (chem/module_dep_simple.F, WRF v4.8.0): the seven land-use x season surface-resistance tables as dep_init expands them over the 25 USGS categories, the six-class ixxxlu simplification the Erisman branches key off, and the five per-gas constants for the RADM2 KPP mechanism (chem_opt = 101).\n\nEvery number here is the instrumented dump of the array the running model actually holds, not a transcription of the printed Wesely tables. That matters: dep_init does not lay the 11 Wesely categories down verbatim, it applies per-category season overrides (USGS 10 Savanna and 13 Evergreen broadleaf are ALWAYS summer, 12 Deciduous needleleaf has modified autumn and winter, 24 Snow/Ice is ALWAYS winter), and it guards water and wetland ground resistance at 1 s/m where the printed table has 0. A component built from the paper gets those cells wrong.\n\nGas slots follow WRF's own p_* numbering for this mechanism so that an index here is directly comparable with a WRF dump; slot 1 is the unused 'not present' slot."
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NUSGS": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 25,
      "description": "Number of USGS land-use categories, nlu."
    },
    "NSEASON": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 5,
      "description": "Number of seasonal categories, dep_seasons."
    },
    "NGAS": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 44,
      "description": "Number of gas slots, numgas = 44 for chem_opt = 101."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "usgs": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NUSGS"
    },
    "season": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NSEASON"
    },
    "gas": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NGAS"
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "WRFWeselyData": {
      "variables": {
        "ri_table": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "usgs",
            "season"
          ],
          "units": "s/m",
          "description": "Minimum bulk canopy stomatal resistance ri(iland,iseason), Wesely (1989) Table 2 as dep_init expands it over the 25 USGS categories. Transcribed from chem/module_dep_simple.F of WRF v4.8.0 via the instrumented dump of the expanded array, so it carries dep_init's per-category season overrides (USGS 10 and 13 are always summer, 12 has modified autumn/winter, 24 is always winter) rather than a naive Wesely-category lookup. The sentinel for 'no path' is 0.10E+11."
        },
        "rlu_table": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "usgs",
            "season"
          ],
          "units": "s/m",
          "description": "Outer-surface (cuticle) resistance of leaves rlu(iland,iseason). Transcribed from chem/module_dep_simple.F of WRF v4.8.0 via the instrumented dump of the expanded array, so it carries dep_init's per-category season overrides (USGS 10 and 13 are always summer, 12 has modified autumn/winter, 24 is always winter) rather than a naive Wesely-category lookup. The sentinel for 'no path' is 0.10E+11."
        },
        "rac_table": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "usgs",
            "season"
          ],
          "units": "s/m",
          "description": "In-canopy aerodynamic resistance rac(iland,iseason). Transcribed from chem/module_dep_simple.F of WRF v4.8.0 via the instrumented dump of the expanded array, so it carries dep_init's per-category season overrides (USGS 10 and 13 are always summer, 12 has modified autumn/winter, 24 is always winter) rather than a naive Wesely-category lookup. The sentinel for 'no path' is 0.10E+11."
        },
        "rgss_table": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "usgs",
            "season"
          ],
          "units": "s/m",
          "description": "Ground-surface resistance for SO2, rgss(iland,iseason). Transcribed from chem/module_dep_simple.F of WRF v4.8.0 via the instrumented dump of the expanded array, so it carries dep_init's per-category season overrides (USGS 10 and 13 are always summer, 12 has modified autumn/winter, 24 is always winter) rather than a naive Wesely-category lookup. The sentinel for 'no path' is 0.10E+11."
        },
        "rgso_table": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "usgs",
            "season"
          ],
          "units": "s/m",
          "description": "Ground-surface resistance for O3, rgso(iland,iseason). Transcribed from chem/module_dep_simple.F of WRF v4.8.0 via the instrumented dump of the expanded array, so it carries dep_init's per-category season overrides (USGS 10 and 13 are always summer, 12 has modified autumn/winter, 24 is always winter) rather than a naive Wesely-category lookup. The sentinel for 'no path' is 0.10E+11."
        },
        "rcls_table": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "usgs",
            "season"
          ],
          "units": "s/m",
          "description": "Lower-canopy resistance for SO2, rcls(iland,iseason). Transcribed from chem/module_dep_simple.F of WRF v4.8.0 via the instrumented dump of the expanded array, so it carries dep_init's per-category season overrides (USGS 10 and 13 are always summer, 12 has modified autumn/winter, 24 is always winter) rather than a naive Wesely-category lookup. The sentinel for 'no path' is 0.10E+11."
        },
        "rclo_table": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "usgs",
            "season"
          ],
          "units": "s/m",
          "description": "Lower-canopy resistance for O3, rclo(iland,iseason). Transcribed from chem/module_dep_simple.F of WRF v4.8.0 via the instrumented dump of the expanded array, so it carries dep_init's per-category season overrides (USGS 10 and 13 are always summer, 12 has modified autumn/winter, 24 is always winter) rather than a naive Wesely-category lookup. The sentinel for 'no path' is 0.10E+11."
        },
        "ixxxlu_table": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "usgs"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The SIX-class simplification of the 25 USGS categories that the Erisman SO2 and NH3 branches key off (chem/module_dep_simple.F:4038-4064, the mminlu = 'USGS' block): 1 urban/bare, 2 agricultural, 3 grassland, 4 deciduous, 5 coniferous/mixed, 6 other, and 0 for water (16) and permanent ice (24), which have their own branches. Distinct from iland, and not the Wesely 11-category index either."
        },
        "hstar_table": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "gas"
          ],
          "units": "M/atm",
          "description": "Effective Henry's law constant H* at 298 K, hstar(n) (M/atm). Zero marks a gas that rc() leaves at Rc = 1; for RADM2 those are HO and HO2, whose Rc the driver then sets to 0 outright so they deposit at the aerodynamic limit. Indexed by WRF's own p_* gas number for chem_opt = 101 (RADM2 KPP): slot 1 is unused, 2 = so2, 3 = sulf, 4 = no2, 5 = no, 6 = o3, 7 = hno3, 8 = h2o2, 9 = ald, 10 = hcho, 11 = op1, 12 = op2, 13 = paa, 14 = ora1, 15 = ora2, 16 = nh3, 17 = n2o5, 18 = no3, 19 = pan, 20 = hc3, 21 = hc5, 22 = hc8, 23 = eth, 24 = co, 25 = ol2, 26 = olt, 27 = oli, 28 = tol, 29 = xyl, 30 = aco3, 31 = tpan, 32 = hono, 33 = hno4, 34 = ket, 35 = gly, 36 = mgly, 37 = dcb, 38 = onit, 39 = csl, 40 = iso, 41 = co2, 42 = ch4, 43 = ho, 44 = ho2. Values are the instrumented dump of the arrays dep_init actually builds for this mechanism."
        },
        "f0_table": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "gas"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Normalized reactivity f0(n), 0, 0.1 or 1. Indexed by WRF's own p_* gas number for chem_opt = 101 (RADM2 KPP): slot 1 is unused, 2 = so2, 3 = sulf, 4 = no2, 5 = no, 6 = o3, 7 = hno3, 8 = h2o2, 9 = ald, 10 = hcho, 11 = op1, 12 = op2, 13 = paa, 14 = ora1, 15 = ora2, 16 = nh3, 17 = n2o5, 18 = no3, 19 = pan, 20 = hc3, 21 = hc5, 22 = hc8, 23 = eth, 24 = co, 25 = ol2, 26 = olt, 27 = oli, 28 = tol, 29 = xyl, 30 = aco3, 31 = tpan, 32 = hono, 33 = hno4, 34 = ket, 35 = gly, 36 = mgly, 37 = dcb, 38 = onit, 39 = csl, 40 = iso, 41 = co2, 42 = ch4, 43 = ho, 44 = ho2. Values are the instrumented dump of the arrays dep_init actually builds for this mechanism."
        },
        "dhr_table": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "gas"
          ],
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Temperature coefficient -dH/R of the Henry's law constant, dhr(n) (K). Used as hstary = hstar exp(dhr (t0-T)/(t0 T)) with t0 = 298 K. The existing AtmosphericDeposition.jl-derived component has no equivalent at all; for SO2 (dhr = 5816) it is a factor of 2.78 at 283 K and 0.39 at 313 K. Indexed by WRF's own p_* gas number for chem_opt = 101 (RADM2 KPP): slot 1 is unused, 2 = so2, 3 = sulf, 4 = no2, 5 = no, 6 = o3, 7 = hno3, 8 = h2o2, 9 = ald, 10 = hcho, 11 = op1, 12 = op2, 13 = paa, 14 = ora1, 15 = ora2, 16 = nh3, 17 = n2o5, 18 = no3, 19 = pan, 20 = hc3, 21 = hc5, 22 = hc8, 23 = eth, 24 = co, 25 = ol2, 26 = olt, 27 = oli, 28 = tol, 29 = xyl, 30 = aco3, 31 = tpan, 32 = hono, 33 = hno4, 34 = ket, 35 = gly, 36 = mgly, 37 = dcb, 38 = onit, 39 = csl, 40 = iso, 41 = co2, 42 = ch4, 43 = ho, 44 = ho2. Values are the instrumented dump of the arrays dep_init actually builds for this mechanism."
        },
        "dratio_table": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "gas"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Ratio of the molecular diffusivity of water vapour to that of the gas, dratio(n) = 0.242/dvj(n). Indexed by WRF's own p_* gas number for chem_opt = 101 (RADM2 KPP): slot 1 is unused, 2 = so2, 3 = sulf, 4 = no2, 5 = no, 6 = o3, 7 = hno3, 8 = h2o2, 9 = ald, 10 = hcho, 11 = op1, 12 = op2, 13 = paa, 14 = ora1, 15 = ora2, 16 = nh3, 17 = n2o5, 18 = no3, 19 = pan, 20 = hc3, 21 = hc5, 22 = hc8, 23 = eth, 24 = co, 25 = ol2, 26 = olt, 27 = oli, 28 = tol, 29 = xyl, 30 = aco3, 31 = tpan, 32 = hono, 33 = hno4, 34 = ket, 35 = gly, 36 = mgly, 37 = dcb, 38 = onit, 39 = csl, 40 = iso, 41 = co2, 42 = ch4, 43 = ho, 44 = ho2. Values are the instrumented dump of the arrays dep_init actually builds for this mechanism."
        },
        "scpr23_table": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "gas"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "(Sc/Pr)^(2/3) with Sc = 0.15/dvj(n) and Pr = 0.72, scpr23(n). NOTE the code uses Pr = 0.72 even though the comment above depvel still claims Sc = 1.15, Pr = 1.0, SCPR23 = 1.10 (FORTRAN_BUGS B6). Indexed by WRF's own p_* gas number for chem_opt = 101 (RADM2 KPP): slot 1 is unused, 2 = so2, 3 = sulf, 4 = no2, 5 = no, 6 = o3, 7 = hno3, 8 = h2o2, 9 = ald, 10 = hcho, 11 = op1, 12 = op2, 13 = paa, 14 = ora1, 15 = ora2, 16 = nh3, 17 = n2o5, 18 = no3, 19 = pan, 20 = hc3, 21 = hc5, 22 = hc8, 23 = eth, 24 = co, 25 = ol2, 26 = olt, 27 = oli, 28 = tol, 29 = xyl, 30 = aco3, 31 = tpan, 32 = hono, 33 = hno4, 34 = ket, 35 = gly, 36 = mgly, 37 = dcb, 38 = onit, 39 = csl, 40 = iso, 41 = co2, 42 = ch4, 43 = ho, 44 = ho2. Values are the instrumented dump of the arrays dep_init actually builds for this mechanism."
        }
      },
